From 542a7f150f3f0a108b13ea9f81807d3a1c7a7c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Terra Ferrao <victor.terra@synkar.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:40:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] can: rockchip_canfd: run IRQ as hardirq on PREEMPT_RT

On PREEMPT_RT the shared CAN interrupt is force-threaded
(irq/NNN-can0). When the IRQ thread finishes it runs pending
softirqs via __local_bh_enable_ip, and in that context a NET_TX
softirq that reaches rkcanfd_start_xmit -> can_put_echo_skb ->
skb_clone can hit the SLUB slowpath, whose rt_spin_lock tries to
schedule with a broken preempt count, producing:

  BUG: scheduling while atomic: irq/148-can0/...
  softirq: huh, entered softirq 2 NET_TX ... with preempt_count
  00000000, exited with ffffffff?

The handler is hardirq-safe by design (that is how it runs on
non-RT kernels): registers, raw spinlocks, GFP_ATOMIC skb
allocations and netif_rx only. Request the IRQ with IRQF_NO_THREAD
so on PREEMPT_RT it stays a true hardirq and the NET_TX softirq it
raises runs in ksoftirqd with correct sleeping-lock semantics
instead of the broken forced-thread tail.

Signed-off-by: Victor Terra Ferrao <victor.terra@synkar.com>

diff --git a/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c b/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
index 6207584..f55c854 100644
--- a/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
@@ -737,7 +737,8 @@ static int rkcanfd_open(struct net_device *ndev)
 	rkcanfd_chip_start(priv);
 	can_rx_offload_enable(&priv->offload);
 
-	err = request_irq(ndev->irq, rkcanfd_irq, IRQF_SHARED, ndev->name, priv);
+	err = request_irq(ndev->irq, rkcanfd_irq, IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_NO_THREAD,
+			  ndev->name, priv);
 	if (err)
 		goto out_rkcanfd_chip_stop;
 
-- 
